      "The new paradigm begins with a single, world-altering premise: there is enough. There is enough food to feed every human being on earth — the FAO estimates that the world produces 1.5 times the food needed to nourish the global population. There is enough water, properly managed and equitably distributed. There is enough land, fairly organised, for every person to have a home. There is enough solar energy reaching the earth's surface in one hour to power global civilisation for a year. There is enough human creativity, ingenuity, and compassion to solve every problem that the old world has treated as inevitable.",
