      "The biblical prophetic tradition is not a collection of predictions. It is a framework for truth-telling: for naming what is real when the institutions around you insist on what is false; for maintaining the vision of what is right when the systems of power are organised around what is wrong; and for holding open the possibility of transformation when every existing structure argues for the inevitability of the status quo. This is why the prophetic tradition resonates with the documented case of this foundation: because Dr McLean's thirty-five-year advocacy is, in its structure, its function, and its evidence base, a prophetic act in the precise technical sense of the term.",
